00:28:45.720 --> 00:28:46.720
Like, two different codes.

00:28:47.020 --> 00:29:00.160
Okay. And the way that it works is that if the checksums all come back good, as you put the game into, like, a real NES hardware, it'll load up the option B, which is, like, the full game.

00:29:00.160 --> 00:29:07.780
Okay. And option A, which is programmed first for a reason, is just this screen with a message that I will read.

00:29:08.120 --> 00:29:13.360
The message is, I would like to thank you for your interest in my game.

00:29:13.800 --> 00:29:17.840
